The changed code adds a `user_can_view_page` check to `render_object_structure`, but the `render_object_edit`/`render_object_preview` views (which share `render_object_endpoint` and render PageContent objects via admin_manager) still fetch the page content and render it without any view-restriction check. The PR's own new tests assert these edit/preview endpoints should return 404 for a staff user with no view permission — exposing that the code path they test does not enforce it.

